  "fixedSourceFindings": [
    {
      "claim": "Tracker timestamp is elapsedRealtime milliseconds, comparable to raw/fixture elapsedRealtime on the same device. Duration is finishElapsed-startElapsed; inferred finish is not layout completion.",
      "source": "ImeTrackerService.java:124-160,390-394,676-715,726-759"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Completed history is an insertion-ordered buffer of completed entries; printed order is not start order. Sequence7 timeout printed after sequence12 is not a later-starting request. Buffer capacity200 does not prove history retained every lifecycle event.",
      "source": "ImeTrackerService.java:433-454,529-544"
    },
    {
      "claim": "STATUS_CANCEL records termination of the tracking entry at its phase. This source does not perform a rollback of rendered IME UI or raw input regions; cancellation must not be equated with hidden keyboard or failed raw sample.",
      "source": "ImeTrackerService.java:296-298,704-715"
    },
    {
      "claim": "IMS resetStateForNewConfiguration removes Insets callback, calls initViews, restarts active input and may re-show via showWindowWithToken(RESET_NEW_CONFIGURATION). That token is TYPE_SHOW/ORIGIN_IME. This is a specific UI-rebuild mechanism consistent with the historical reset label before the positive callback.",
      "source": "InputMethodService.java:1909-1955,3056-3059,4525-4528"
    },
    {
      "claim": "SettingsObserver uses the IME main-looper Handler. Target URI callback reads the setting and unconditionally calls reset; it does not compare old/new setting or resource Configuration.",
      "source": "InputMethodService.java:1583-1585,1631-1644"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The alternative Configuration callback resets only after initialization when diffPublicOnly(newConfig) contains unhandled changes and CONFIG_RESOURCES_UNUSED is absent. First comparison can use CONFIG_CHANGED=-1 if no known Configuration. The observed same final Configuration in both arms does not reveal all intermediate values, lastKnownConfig or handled flags.",
      "source": "ImsConfigurationTracker.java:38-47,65-72,87-107"
    },
    {
      "claim": "LatinIME onComputeInsets can return before input view/visible keyboard/suggestion view exists, and uses shown state and geometry to populate REGION. ViewRoot traversal recomputes insets and sends setInsets when changed/pending. Existing records do not timestamp these internals.",
      "source": "LatinIME.java:1245-1283; ViewRootImpl.java:4705-4768"
    },
    {
      "claim": "No fixed dictionary-ready guard appears in LatinIME onComputeInsets. The cached two-second dictionary wait message logs timeout; dictionary availability callback updates availability/suggestions. Dictionary/cache work can still be a hypothesis, but current data do not establish it as the eight-second cause.",
      "source": "LatinIME.java:126,286-312,359-368,691-702,1003-1064,1245-1283"
    }
  ],
